{"name": "propose_test", "arguments": {"name": "Consumer Messaging Test for Differentiated Hearing Protection", "theories": ["T1", "T2"], "method": "Online survey with randomized messaging exposure. Participants are recruited from a panel of adults who have purchased hearing protection in the past 12 months. Participants are randomly assigned to one of three conditions: (A) standard safety message emphasizing EN 352 compliance and workplace use; (B) lifestyle message emphasizing fashion, comfort, and multiple color options; (C) high\u2011risk use case message emphasizing EN 352 compliance for construction, industrial, and loud environments. After viewing the assigned message, participants indicate their willingness to pay a premium over the standard price point and",
"sample": "400 adult respondents (200 per condition) from a panel that has purchased hearing protection in the past 12 months.", "measure": "Willingness to pay (WTP) premium over the standard price point (EUR) and purchase intent (binary: would purchase).", "prediction_by_theory": {"T1": "Condition B (lifestyle) will show the highest WTP premium and purchase intent compared to Condition A and C.", "T2": "Condition C (high\u2011risk) will show the highest WTP premium and purchase intent compared to Condition A and B."}, "decision_rule": "If the WTP premium for Condition B is at least 1.5x the premium for Condition A and at least 1.5x the premium for Condition C, proceed to develop a differentiated consumer proposition targeting lifestyle. If the WTP premium for Condition C is at least 1.5x the premium for Condition A and at least 1.5x the premium for Condition B, proceed to develop a differentiated consumer proposition targeting high\u2011",
"cost_eur": 15000, "weeks": 8}}

